', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/9697.jpeg', N'Since the launch of the safety recognition program in April 2025, CCM’s Total Recordable Injury Frequency (TRIF) has decreased significantly, dropping from 16.9 to 9.67. This reduction reflects a meaningful improvement in safety performance, indicating that the changes implemented have positively influenced worker behavior and the effectiveness of safety practices at the site.', NULL, N'The decline in TRIF suggests that the safety recognition program has been effective in reducing the frequency of recordable injuries and improving overall safety performance at CCM, though continued effort is needed to sustain and further improve these results.', N'The program had a measurable positive impact on CCM’s safety performance, as reflected in the reduction in TRIF. This initiative demonstrated that actively recognizing and reinforcing safe behaviors can positively influence worker engagement and safety performance. ', 0, NULL, N'.', '2026-04-28T00:00:00.000', '2026-04-29T08:13:05.000', N'200959', NULL, NULL);
