However, risk data remained underutilized, with limited capability to generate portfolio-level insights, identify systemic risks, or support proactive decision-making.
Reporting was manual, time-consuming, and primarily descriptive, focusing on individual project updates rather than portfolio-level trends and root causes.
The absence of automation and advanced analytics, including AI-supported analysis, limited the organization’s ability to transform available data into timely insights for leadership.', N'To leverage standardized risk practices across Ontario Surface Projects and implement an AI‑enabled, automated process to generate monthly portfolio insights, enabling proactive, data‑driven decision-making and improved visibility of systemic risks.', N'10110', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/10012.jpeg', N'Standardized risk data implemented in 2025 was underutilized. It remained focused on static reporting, limiting insights, trend analysis, and proactive decision-making.', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/10012.jpeg', N'Implemented AI‑supported analysis and automated a monthly risk newsletter, transforming standardized data into portfolio insights, improving efficiency, visibility, and decision-making.', N'https://globalvale-my.sharepoint.com/:f:/g/personal/aidilma_ferreira_vale_com/IgDIlz0FGyGjTazNnR-ABh3oAahPsqNkzi_MGlSYiWy34yU?e=5BMkPL', N'Yes. The initiative successfully transformed standardized risk data into automated, AI-supported portfolio insights. Existing reporting tools were enhanced through structured analysis and automated insight generation, improving efficiency, visibility, and the ability to proactively identify systemic risks and support leadership decision-making.', N'Standardized processes provide a strong foundation for data quality and consistency. Additional value can be unlocked by combining this foundation with structured analysis, automation, and AI to generate actionable portfolio insights.', 0, NULL, N'Essa padronização trouxe maior clareza e assertividade na tomada de decisão, permitindo a definição mais eficiente da estratégia de planejamento das atividades. Como resultado, houve ganho significativo no processo de categorização das demandas: o tempo médio de classificação, que anteriormente era de cerca de 10 minutos, foi reduzido para aproximadamente 30 segundos,  à padronização aplicada já no momento de abertura da nota pelo inspetor', '2026-05-12T00:00:00.000', '2026-05-13T16:07:34.000', N'81040307', NULL, NULL);
